sequenceDiagram
  %% A container clone's removal on the Gateway engine (ADR 0271, docs/reference/gateway-engine.md#instancedestroy, docs/reference/instance-removal.md): what #4211 shipped, InstanceDestroyEngineFlow with one step `remove` running the executor's `instance.destroy` (apps/agent/crates/instance/src/destroy.rs). Every other removal is instance/destroy.mmd on Swamp.
  %% Built, proof pending: a clone that owns private Routes withdraws them on the engine first, with the primitives of route/engine/destroy.mmd.
  %% status: built
  %% command: instance:destroy
  %% kind: instance.destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>executor
  CLI->>GW: instance:destroy 42<br/>--yes --force
  Note over GW: Validate, capture the set<br/>Instance 42 · task #5132
  %%> Same admission as instance/destroy.mmd: consent, captures, Schedule trigger removal, then the removal intent in one transaction that marks Instance 42 removing
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
    %%> - `instance.destroy` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`, and the Node reports `instance.destroy` in `$KV.NODES`, independently of `instance.create`
    %%> - InstanceDestroyEngineFlow accepts the plan, all of it checked against the saved intent:
    %%> - the target is an Instance with a positive ID, equal to the intent's `instance_id` and, checked on its own, to `container_destroy.instance_id`, the field that becomes the signed step's target; a plan that names 43 there refuses; the Operation's Node is positive and equals both the intent's and the saved plan's `node_id`
    %%> - development, `--force`, not the default name; a positive clone source that is not the Instance itself
    %%> - no `after_operation_id` (no wait for a create or completion) and no CI hold
    %%> - exactly one member, and it is this Instance, with `run_teardown: false`; the plan's Routes are an empty list
    %%> - a member `route_id` or `additional_route_ids` only for private Routes with no LAN rule or Ingress edge, whose whole after-state the admission rendered (`route_engine`: each Node's Caddyfile, changed shared pools and DNS files without the Routes, with the digests of the files they replace); a PHP version whose pool empties refuses; every VPN Node with a DNS change reports `dns.guarded_records` and each serving Node `route.withdraw_site`
    %%> - exactly one teardown entry, for this Instance, with no steps; no Processes, Schedules, database connections, database servers or SQLite files
    %%> - the saved identity is the signed contract: container and ACL `instance-42`, project `orbit-instances` or `orbit-instances-nested`, pool `orbit-instances`, mirror `/var/lib/orbit/instance-repositories/42.git`, firewall prefix `orbit:instance-42-`, the asleep marker, inner volume `inner-42` when present
    %%> - else `EngineUnsupported`, and the whole removal runs on Swamp
    Note over GW: Bind remove, take the lock<br/>commit, publish the start
    %%> The Gateway binds step `remove` (budget 600 s, resend 15 s) and the Instance's Operation lock in one transaction before it publishes the start
    %%> Cancel still works during order preparation, deadline scheduling and the Node consumer's setup; just before the first publish the Gateway checks cancel and records the first order's signed expiry under the same lock
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5132
    opt clone owns a Route
      EN->>N: Withdraw the Route first<br/>route/engine/destroy steps
      %%> `dns-node` (guarded `dns.publish_records`), then `withdraw-node` (`route.withdraw_site`) and `sibling-node` (a TLS probe of another Route on that Node), with no DNS grace (a destroyed name has no new target, as instance/destroy.mmd decides)
      %%> Every step is receipt-bound like `remove`: a lost receipt resends the same step, the Node's journal answers its stored result, and the Instance stays fenced until a terminal receipt
      %%> A retry of a removal whose earlier run withdrew the Route (`route_withdrawn`) has none of these steps, as the Swamp run skips its withdraw
      Note over EN: Record the withdrawal<br/>free the Route Nodes
      %%> Gateway step `release`, as the Swamp run's release step: `route_withdrawn_at` on the removal, then the Route withdrawal holds go
      %%> `remove` waits for it; a failed withdrawal fails the Operation as `route.withdrawal_failed` at "Withdraw the Route" (removal step `route_target_clear`) before the container is touched
    end
    EN->>N: Remove the clone<br/>instance.destroy · step remove
    %%> Input: `project`, `name`, `pool`, `acl`, `inner_volume`; the executor checks it again (`instance.destroy_input_invalid`)
    %%> Holds the same target lock as sleep and wake; checks that `instance-42` is a container on the admitted pool
    %%> Force-stops it unless Incus reports Stopped (`instance.removal_stop_failed`), deletes it with `--force`; a failed delete restores the snapshots' missing datasets and deletes again
    %%> Removes the inner volume and its owned unused `build-` and `spare-` volumes, then the ACL
    %%> Read-back: the container, the ACL and every owned volume are gone, else `instance.removal_incomplete`
    %%> Then the `orbit:instance-42-` ufw rules: an owned rule that shares its specification with a foreign rule refuses (`instance.removal_incomplete`); each is deleted by specification and their absence is read back
    %%> Then the power helper's legacy `discard` (`instance.power_discard_failed`), then the mail folder, the mirror, `/var/tmp/orbit-task-base-42` and the hibernation asleep, cold, log and awake files; an absent one counts as removed
    %%> Last, the executor discards its own freeze state for Instance 42 (`discard_destroyed`); a failure there is `instance.power_discard_failed`, never success
    N-->>EN: One terminal receipt<br/>after the whole sequence
    %%> Sent only after every part above held, or with the first failure's code; the executor appends its `done` record first. A refusal such as `instance.removal_dataset_taken` is kept as a result too
    opt the receipt is lost
      EN->>N: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
      %%> The journal repeats the stored result with `repeat: true`; the deletion never runs twice
      %%> A lost acknowledgement, cancel, expiry or order refusal never releases the Instance lock: none proves the Node did not act. An `expired` refusal keeps the fence and the scheduled retry
      %%> Resends stop once one could expire after the first order's expiry minus 10 s plus 24 h of journal retention; then Instance 42 stays fenced until a matching terminal receipt or authoritative recovery; an absent record after compaction settles nothing
      N-->>EN: Stored result<br/>repeat: true
    end
    %%> A receipt counts only when its Node, Operation step ID, action and target match
    alt the removal held
      EN->>GW: Project the removal<br/>applyEngine
      %%> DevelopmentInstanceDestroyProjection::applyEngine records the same removal as a Swamp run: Instance 42 and its records are deleted, task #5132 succeeds
    else a terminal failure
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
      Note over GW: Keep Instance, mark failed<br/>removal intent kept
      %%> `error.detail` is a bounded, redacted tail of whole lines, or says the diagnostic was omitted
      %%> Retry: the same command; the existing retry rules apply
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-instance-destroy
    %%> The kind is not enabled, the Node lacks `instance.destroy`, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole removal runs instance/destroy.mmd; an Operation never splits across engines
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
